      "position": 0,
      "content": "Resources",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e9ce6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "See the University Catalog for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. See the Admissions website for transfer admission requirements/information. See the International Education &amp; Global Engagement website for international transfer academic qualifications. See the Academic Advising Programs website for information on California Promise and Associate Degree for Transfer. See the University Catalog for Credit by Exam information (AP, IB, CLEP).",
      "contentHtml": "<ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://catalog.csuchico.edu/archive/2025-2026/colleges-departments/college-humanities-fine-arts/languages-cultures/spanish-ba/#programrequirementstext\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">University Catalog</a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> for the full listing of degree requirements for this major.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://www.csuchico.edu/admissions/transfer/index.shtml\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Admissions </a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">website for transfer admission requirements/information.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://www.csuchico.edu/international/qualifications/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">International Education &amp; Global Engagement </a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">website for international transfer academic qualifications.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://www.csuchico.edu/aap/programs/index.shtml\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Academic Advising Programs</a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> website for information on California Promise and Associate Degree for Transfer.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://catalog.csuchico.edu/archive/2025-2026/academic-standards-policies/course-credit-policies/#creditbyexternalexamtext\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">University Catalog</a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> for Credit by Exam information (AP, IB, CLEP).</span></li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "id": "d3ce6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "Associate Degree for Transfer Match",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "d9ce6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "The BA in Spanish is an approved match to the AA-T in Spanish.",
      "contentHtml": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The BA in Spanish is an approved match to the AA-T in Spanish.</span></p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "ecce6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 4,
      "content": "Spanish Language Proficiency",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e4ce6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 5,
      "content": "Students with proficiency and/or prior coursework in Spanish should consult the Language and Cultures Department for course placement. In Group 1 below, students select 0-12 units based on placement. Students who have equivalent knowledge in Spanish may challenge intermediate-level language courses (Group 2 below) for credit by enrolling in the class and taking the challenge exam. All students challenging a course must submit an official letter requesting to challenge the course to the Languages and Cultures Department chair by the end of the second week of the semester. See Course Credit Policy for more information.",
      "contentHtml": "<ul><li>Students with proficiency and/or prior coursework in Spanish should consult the Language and Cultures Department for course placement. In Group 1 below, students select 0-12 units based on placement. </li><li>Students who have equivalent knowledge in Spanish may challenge intermediate-level language courses (Group 2 below) for credit by enrolling in the class and taking the challenge exam.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">All students challenging a course must submit an official letter requesting to challenge the course to the Languages and Cultures Department chair by the end of the second week of the semester. </li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">See&nbsp;Course Credit Policy&nbsp;for more information.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "id": "0724be70-7ec1-48ac-91c2-019760095d0a",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 6,
      "content": "Important Note",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0520010d-d155-413f-84f8-019755ce93ba",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 7,
      "content": "This agreement is not a static document. Articulations may be updated or added at any time , and the information provided is subject to change without notice. This agreement does not include upper-division major requirements, course prerequisites, general education coursework, or university-specific graduation requirements necessary for degree completion. Department agreements should be referenced alongside major agreements to ensure a clearer understanding of course articulation and program planning.",
      "contentHtml": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This agreement is not a static document. </span><strong style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Articulations may be updated or added at any time</strong><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">, and the information provided is subject to change without notice.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This agreement does not include upper-division major requirements, course prerequisites, general education coursework, or university-specific graduation requirements necessary for degree completion.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Department agreements should be referenced alongside major agreements to ensure a clearer understanding of course articulation and program planning.</span></p>"
    }
